   def set_next_output(self, output: list[TResponseOutputItem] | Exception):\n        self.turn_outputs.append(output)\n\n    def add_multiple_turn_outputs(self, outputs: list[list[TResponseOutputItem] | Exception]):\n        self.turn_outputs.extend(outputs)\n\n    def get_next_output(self) -> list[TResponseOutputItem] | Exception:\n        if not self.turn_outputs:\n            return []\n        return self.turn_outputs.pop(0)\n\n    async def get_response(\n        self,\n        system_instructions: str | None,\n        input: str | list[TResponseInputItem],\n        model_settings: ModelSettings,\n        tools: list[Tool],\n        output_schema: AgentOutputSchemaBase | None,\n        handoffs: list[Handoff],\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788493649709},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_006f6366410140a5ac0ad919","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Tests\n\nBefore running any tests, make sure you have `uv` installed (and ideally run `make sync` after).\n\n## Running tests\n\n```\nmake tests\n```\n\n## Snapshots\n\nWe use [inline-snapshots](https://15r10nk.github.io/inline-snapshot/latest/) for some tests. If your code adds new snapshot tests or breaks existing ones, you can fix/create them. After fixing/creating snapshots, run `make tests` again to verify the tests pass.\n\n### Fixing snapshots\n\n```\nmake snapshots-fix\n```\n\n### Creating snapshots\n\n```\nmake snapshots-update\n```\n46:    if request.node.get_closest_marker(\"allow_call_model_methods\"):\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788493649709},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No network access presumably. I'll implement based on the user's requirements, matching the upstream PR as best I can recall.\n\nLet me now recall the actual upstream PR #1582 more concretely. Actually, I just remembered — I can look at the actual openai-agents-python code at a recent version. Version 0.0.17 is from ~May 2025. The extra_args PR #1582 was merged June 10, 2