n    model_settings=ModelSettings(temperature=0.1),\n)\n```\n\n## Common issues with using other LLM providers\n\n### Tracing client error 401\n\nIf you get errors related to tracing, this is because traces are uploaded to OpenAI servers, and you don't have an OpenAI API key. You have three options to resolve this:\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788493928534},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5e35be722d4849fc8ad00016","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"```python\nfrom agents import Agent, ModelSettings\n\nenglish_agent = Agent(\n    name=\"English agent\",\n    instructions=\"You only speak English\",\n    model=\"gpt-4o\",\n    model_settings=ModelSettings(temperature=0.1),\n)\n```\n\n### Passing provider-specific parameters\n\nDifferent model providers sometimes have unique parameters that are not covered by the standard\n`ModelSettings` fields. `ModelSettings` accepts an `extra_args` dictionary of arbitrary keyword\narguments that are passed straight through to the underlying model API call, so you can use\nprovider-specific features without waiting for official support.\n\n```python\nfrom agents import Agent, ModelSettings\n\nenglish_agent = Agent(\n    name=\"English agent\",\n    instructions=\"You only speak English\",\n    model=\"gpt-4o\",\n    model_settings=ModelSettings(\n        temperature=0.1,\n        extra_args={\"some_provider_specific_arg\": True},\n    ),\n)\n```\n\n!!! note\n\n    Not all model providers support all parameters, so passing unsupported parameters may cause\n    errors. Please check the API documentation for the specific model and provider you are\n    using. Any `None` values in `extra_args` are filtered out before the request is made, and\n    when model settings are merged (for example, agent settings combined with `RunConfig`\n    settings), the `extra_args` dictionaries are merged together with the more specific settings\n    taking precedence.\n\n## Common issues with using other LLM